# Force GitHub Linguist to classify the engine as HolyC.
# The repo sources carry the HolyC-style uppercase ".HC" extension, but
# Linguist maps HolyC to lowercase ".hc" and otherwise guesses ".H"/".h"
# files as C, so the repo would show up as C. Mark every engine source and
# header as HolyC so the language bar (and the README's HolyC framing) is
# accurate. Python/GIF/MD assets stay as their natural languages.
*.HC linguist-language=HolyC
*.H  linguist-language=HolyC
*.h  linguist-language=HolyC
